{"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting"},"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"role":"collection","title":"DestinationTesting","modules":[{"name":"DestinationTesting"}],"roleHeading":"Framework","externalID":"DestinationTesting","symbolKind":"module"},"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/destinationtesting"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"topicSections":[{"title":"Checking a destination","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup"],"anchor":"Checking-a-destination"},{"title":"Sending without a network","identifiers":["doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport"],"anchor":"Sending-without-a-network"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record."}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" runs the checks every vendor destination must pass, through a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" that keeps each request and answers from a script rather than the network:"}]},{"items":[{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"its requests match recorded fixtures byte for byte;","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" value is sent only after the adopter opts in, and only while the record reveals it;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"behind a tracker’s consent and ","type":"text"},{"code":"accepting(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", it sends exactly the records it is handed;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"a record over the vendor’s limit is left out and reported, and the rest of its batch is sent;","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no response, a 5xx, 408 and 429 are retried, and other failures are dropped and reported;"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"no request carries a trace context in its header fields, even while a tracer is active."}],"type":"paragraph"}]}],"type":"unorderedList"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Make it with the vendor’s limit and a closure that calls the vendor’s factory with the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":"‘s plan, transport and backoff. Every check’s records are tracked at the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"setup’s "},{"code":"timestamp","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":"; a factory whose encoder leaves out records by their age takes it as the time"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"it encodes at, so the checks pass whenever the test runs. Run each "},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" as a test"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"case of its own:"}]},{"code":["import DestinationTesting","import Foundation","import HTTPDestinations","import PostHogEncoding","import Testing","","@Test(arguments: ConformanceCheck.allCases)","func postHogConformance(check: ConformanceCheck) async throws {","    let host = try #require(URL(string: \"https:\/\/posthog.example.com\"))","    let conformance = DestinationConformance(limit: PostHogBatchEncoder.batchLimit) { setup in","        try HTTPDestination.postHog(projectToken: \"phc_test\", host: host, plan: setup.plan, transport: setup.transport, backoff: setup.backoff)","    }","    try await conformance.expect(check)","}"],"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Each check records a Swift Testing issue for every rule the destination breaks. A project’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"tests write their assertions out in full. This one is shared on purpose, as TrackingPlanTesting’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"code":"expectTrackingPlan(_:matches:sourceLocation:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is, so every vendor module runs the same checks."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"It imports Swift Testing, so add it to test targets only. "},{"code":"import Traffluent","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" leaves it out."}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The guide ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"covers the module these checks test.","type":"text"}]}]}],"sections":[],"references":{"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ScriptedTransport":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ScriptedTransport","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/scriptedtransport","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ScriptedTransport","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"An "},{"code":"HTTPTransport","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" that answers each request from a script and keeps every request it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sent: the seam a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance"},{"type":"text","text":" check sends through instead of the network."}],"role":"symbol","title":"ScriptedTransport","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ScriptedTransport","kind":"identifier"}]},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationConformance":{"type":"topic","role":"symbol","kind":"symbol","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DestinationConformance","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"text":"The checks every vendor destination passes, run from the vendor module’s tests: its requests","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"match recorded fixtures byte for byte, and it keeps the library’s rules for ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sensitive"},{"text":" values,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"consent, oversized records, retries and trace context.","type":"text"}],"title":"DestinationConformance","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DestinationConformance","kind":"identifier"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationconformance"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/ConformanceCheck":{"role":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"enum","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConformanceCheck","kind":"identifier"}],"navigatorTitle":[{"text":"ConformanceCheck","kind":"identifier"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"One rule every vendor destination keeps, which "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance\/expect(_:sourceLocation:)"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"checks."}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/ConformanceCheck","title":"ConformanceCheck","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/conformancecheck","kind":"symbol","type":"topic"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting":{"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting","abstract":[{"text":"Check from Swift Testing that a vendor destination keeps the library’s rules and sends what its fixtures record.","type":"text"}],"role":"collection","title":"DestinationTesting","kind":"symbol"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationConformance/expect(_:sourceLocation:)":{"role":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance\/expect(_:sourceLocation:)","title":"expect(_:sourceLocation:)","type":"topic","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"expect","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"(","kind":"text"},{"text":"ConformanceCheck","preciseIdentifier":"s:18DestinationTesting16ConformanceCheckO","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"sourceLocation","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SourceLocation","preciseIdentifier":"s:7Testing14SourceLocationV","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":") ","kind":"text"},{"text":"async","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"throws","kind":"keyword"}],"abstract":[{"text":"Records an issue for each way the destination breaks ","type":"text"},{"code":"check","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"’s rule.","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationconformance\/expect(_:sourcelocation:)"},"doc://DestinationTesting/documentation/DestinationTesting/DestinationSetup":{"type":"topic","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"DestinationSetup","kind":"identifier"}],"url":"\/documentation\/destinationtesting\/destinationsetup","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationSetup","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"What a "},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/DestinationTesting\/documentation\/DestinationTesting\/DestinationConformance"},{"type":"text","text":" check hands the vendor’s factory: the plan of the events it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"sends, the transport to send them through, a backoff short enough that a retry doesn’t hold the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"test up, and when its records were tracked."}],"role":"symbol","title":"DestinationSetup","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DestinationSetup","kind":"identifier"}]},"https://tyler-keith-thompson.github.io/Traffluent/documentation/traffluent/writingavendordestination":{"url":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","type":"link","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/Traffluent\/documentation\/traffluent\/writingavendordestination","title":"Writing a Vendor Destination","titleInlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Writing a Vendor Destination"}]}}}